# "Return a creature you control to its owner's hand" is a cost, so with no creature of your own the Ruse cannot be cast:
# on turn two Bot2 casts an Ornithopter and then a Mox Jet with an Island and a Mox Sapphire open on Bot1's side but no Bot1 creature, and the
# attempted Ruse is reversed against the Mox Jet (a spell, with Bot2's Ornithopter on the battlefield - an opponent's creature does
# not do). On turn three Bot1 casts its own Ornithopter; on turn four the Ruse, with the same mana, returns it to
# counter Bot2's second Ornithopter - any spell, a creature spell here, can be countered.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Island
Mox Sapphire
Ornithopter
Familiar's Ruse
Island
Island
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Jet
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Swamp x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Familiar's Ruse.Cast(Stack.Mox Jet)
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
? Bot1.Hand = Familiar's Ruse; Island; Island; Island; Ornithopter
? Bot1.Life = 20
? Bot1.Mana =
? Bot1.Battlefield = Island; Mox Sapphire
? Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Tapped = false
? Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Tapped = false
? Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
? Bot2.Battlefield = Ornithopter
? Exile.Count = 0
? Stack = Mox Jet
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Familiar's Ruse.Cast(Stack.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Choose(Ornithopter)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot2.Battlefield = Ornithopter; Mox Jet
Bot1.Battlefield = Island; Island; Mox Sapphire
Bot1.Graveyard = Familiar's Ruse
